      "reply_text": "Plan: fit a simple saturating outcome mean with additive cohort shift and Gaussian marker/outcome with stable covariance, then submit.\n```python\nimport numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom scipy.optimize import curve_fit\n\n# prepare experimental data\nexp_fit = exp.copy()\n\n# fit outcome mean: y = a + b*cohort + c*(1-exp(-k*dose))\nX_d = exp_fit[\"dose\"].values.astype(float)\nX_c = exp_fit[\"cohort\"].values.astype(float)\ny = exp_fit[\"outcome\"].values.astype(float)\n\ndef f(X, a, b, c, k):\n    d, coh = X\n    return a + b*coh + c*(1 - np.exp(-k*d))\n\np0 = [0.1, -2.0, 7.5, 0.25]\npars, _ = curve_fit(f, (X_d, X_c), y, p0=p0, maxfev=20000)\na, b, c, k = pars\n\n# marker model: Normal(mean = m0 + m1*cohort, sd = const)\nm_coef = np.polyfit(exp_fit[\"cohort\"].values, exp_fit[\"marker\"].values, 1)\nm1, m0 = m_coef[0], m_coef[1]\n\n# residual covariance for (marker, outcome) after subtracting means\nmu_out = f((X_d, X_c), *pars)\nmu_mark = m0 + m1 * X_c\nres = np.column_stack([exp_fit[\"marker\"].values - mu_mark, exp_fit[\"outcome\"].values - mu_out])\ncov = np.cov(res.T, ddof=1)\n\n# observational natural dose distribution from obs\nobs_dose = obs[\"dose\"].values.astype(float)\n\nprint(\"fitted outcome params:\", pars)\nprint(\"marker mean params m0,m1:\", (m0, m1))\nprint(\"residual cov:\\n\", cov)\nprint(\"obs dose mean/std:\", obs_dose.mean(), obs_dose.std())\n\ncode = f'''\nimport numpy as np, pandas as pd\n\nA = {float(a)!r}\nB = {float(b)!r}\nC = {float(c)!r}\nK = {float(k)!r}\nM0 = {float(m0)!r}\nM1 = {float(m1)!r}\nCOV = np.array({cov.tolist()!r}, dtype=float)\nDOSE_OBS = np.array({obs_dose.tolist()!r}, dtype=float)\n\ndef model(regime, n, seed):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    cohort = float(regime.context.get(\"cohort\", 0.0))\n    if \"dose\" in regime.config:\n        dose = np.full(n, float(regime.config[\"dose\"]), dtype=float)\n    else:\n        dose = rng.choice(DOSE_OBS, size=n, replace=True).astype(float)\n    mu_marker = M0 + M1 * cohort\n    mu_outcome = A + B * cohort + C * (1.0 - np.exp(-K * dose))\n    eps = rng.multivariate_normal(mean=np.zeros(2), cov=COV, size=n)\n    marker = mu_marker + eps[:, 0]\n    outcome = mu_outcome + eps[:, 1]\n    return pd.DataFrame({{\"dose\": dose.astype(float), \"marker\": marker.astype(float), \"outcome\": outcome.astype(float)}})\n'''\n\nres = env.submit(code)\nprint(\"accepted:\", res.accepted)\nprint(\"error:\", getattr(res, \"error\", None))\n```",
